## Exact roadmap grammar

Start `roadmap_markdown` with `<!-- oxide-roadmap-schema:1 -->` and exactly one fenced `toml`
block using this field set. Oxide canonicalizes field order and only the phase and set-like
collections named above after parsing; it preserves authored narrative-list order.

<!-- oxide-roadmap-schema:1 -->
```toml
schema = 1
title = "Roadmap"
status = "ready"
specification_root = "path/from/the/supplied/corpus"

[[global_invariants]]
id = "oxide-verification-policy"
statement = "Production logic has meaningful contracts, component refinement, complete coverage, and exact-tree composition; trusted effects remain narrow and policy-free."
sources = []

[[stages]]
id = "capability-id"
outcome = "One concise capability outcome."
included_scope = ["Concrete owned scope."]
excluded_scope = []
dependencies = []
source_specifications = [
  { path = "docs/specs/PRODUCT.md", anchor = "Exact heading title", requirement = "Exact contiguous source quotation." },
]
applicable_global_invariants = ["oxide-verification-policy"]
implementation_goals = ["Implement the owned capability and its contracts."]
verification_goals = ["Prove the named logical property under its declared assumptions."]
readiness = "ready"
```

Values illustrate grammar only; copy none without source support except the mandated policy
invariant.

Top level contains only `schema`, `title`, `status`, `specification_root`, invariants, and stages.
Each invariant has only `id`, `statement`, `sources`; each phase only the ten fields shown. Add no
priority, rationale, notes, or acceptance field. Use explicit empty arrays, unique IDs, and only
`planned`, `ready`, `deferred`, or `blocked` readiness.

